---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const faqSchema = {
 "@context": "https://schema.org",
 "@type": "FAQPage",
 "mainEntity": [
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "How long does a DNS migration take?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "The DNS change itself is instant at the authoritative server. Propagation takes one old-TTL cycle: minutes with TTL 300, up to 48 hours for nameserver changes."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Can I migrate without downtime?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Yes, by lowering TTL ahead of time and keeping the old server running during the transition window."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What breaks most often during migration?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Missing records (MX, TXT for verification), forgetting to lower TTL, and decommissioning the old server too early."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Do I need to change nameservers to migrate DNS?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Only if you’re switching DNS providers. If you’re just changing A records at the same host, nameservers stay the same."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Should I export my DNS records first?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Yes: always have a backup before any migration. Most providers offer an export option, or use the record lookup to capture current values."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What is the biggest migration mistake?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Decommissioning the old server before propagation completes. Cached answers still point there, and users hit a dead server."
   }
  }
 ]
}
---
<BaseLayout
  title="DNS Migration Checklist | PromptDNS"
  description="dns migration checklist"
  schema={[faqSchema]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/dns/" class="hover:text-accent">DNS Guide</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">The Complete DNS Migration Checklist</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">The Complete DNS Migration Checklist</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Every step for a zero-downtime DNS migration, ordered by when to do it: from lowering TTLs to decommissioning the old server.</p>
    <div class="rich-text mt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">24+ hours before: preparation</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li class="leading-relaxed">Lower TTL on ALL records you’ll change to 300 seconds.</li><li class="leading-relaxed">Export and back up every record from the current DNS host.</li><li class="leading-relaxed">Create the zone at the new provider and verify it answers identically.</li><li class="leading-relaxed">Keep the old server running: it must serve traffic during the transition.</li></ul>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">At cutover: make the change</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li class="leading-relaxed">Update records at the new provider (not the old one).</li><li class="leading-relaxed">Change nameservers at the registrar if switching providers.</li><li class="leading-relaxed">Test with the propagation checker until resolvers agree.</li></ul>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">After: cleanup</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li class="leading-relaxed">Raise TTLs back to 3600 on stable records.</li><li class="leading-relaxed">Flush local caches on test devices.</li><li class="leading-relaxed">Keep the old server live for 48 hours (NS delegation window) before decommissioning.</li><li class="leading-relaxed">Update your documentation with the new provider details.</li></ul>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How long does a DNS migration take?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">The DNS change itself is instant at the authoritative server. Propagation takes one old-TTL cycle: minutes with TTL 300, up to 48 hours for nameserver changes.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Can I migrate without downtime?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Yes, by lowering TTL ahead of time and keeping the old server running during the transition window.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What breaks most often during migration?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Missing records (MX, TXT for verification), forgetting to lower TTL, and decommissioning the old server too early.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Do I need to change nameservers to migrate DNS?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Only if you’re switching DNS providers. If you’re just changing A records at the same host, nameservers stay the same.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Should I export my DNS records first?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Yes: always have a backup before any migration. Most providers offer an export option, or use the record lookup to capture current values.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What is the biggest migration mistake?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Decommissioning the old server before propagation completes. Cached answers still point there, and users hit a dead server.</p></details></div>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Related</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-2"><li><a href="/dns-propagation/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">DNS propagation explained →</a></li><li><a href="/what-is-ttl-in-dns/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">TTL explained →</a></li><li><a href="/dns-propagation-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">Propagation checker →</a></li></ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
